{
  "_comment": [
    "HAND-WRITTEN. Do not generate this file from validator output: an expectation",
    "derived from the thing it checks asserts only self-consistency, which is worth",
    "nothing. Each entry states what the mesh was built to exhibit.",
    "",
    "`load` is `ok` or `reject`. For `reject`, `error_contains` must appear in the",
    "error message. For `ok`, any of the boolean/count fields present are asserted;",
    "if `findings` is present it is exhaustive, so a finding kind that is absent",
    "from the map must not occur (self-intersections excepted; they have their own",
    "field, because the exact pair count depends on tessellation).",
    "",
    "Every mesh here goes through binary STL, so vertex counts are post-weld and",
    "unused vertices cannot survive: STL stores triangles, not a vertex table."
  ],
