    {
      "_why": "Three triangles share one edge, so that edge has three incident faces. The six outer edges of the fan are boundaries. No edge has exactly two uses, so orientation consistency is vacuously true.",
      "file": "broken-nonmanifold.stl", "units": "mm", "load": "ok",
      "is_manifold": false, "is_watertight": false,
      "is_orientation_consistent": true, "is_solid": false,
      "triangles": 3, "vertices": 5, "components": 1,
      "findings": { "non-manifold-edge": 1, "boundary-edge": 6 }
    },
    {
      "_why": "A cube with one facet removed leaves a triangular hole: three boundary edges. A boundary edge is also non-manifold, since it has one incident face rather than two.",
      "file": "broken-open.stl", "units": "mm", "load": "ok",
      "is_manifold": false, "is_watertight": false,
      "is_orientation_consistent": true, "is_solid": false,
      "triangles": 11, "vertices": 8, "components": 1,
      "findings": { "boundary-edge": 3 }
    },
    {
      "_why": "One facet wound backwards. Its three edges are each then traversed in the same direction by both incident triangles. Still closed and manifold: only the winding is wrong.",
      "file": "broken-flipped-face.stl", "units": "mm", "load": "ok",
      "is_manifold": true, "is_watertight": true,
      "is_orientation_consistent": false, "is_solid": false,
      "triangles": 12, "vertices": 8, "components": 1,
      "findings": { "inconsistent-orientation": 3 }
    },
    {
      "_why": "Every facet wound backwards. Locally consistent everywhere, globally inside out, so it is caught by the sign of the enclosed volume rather than by the edge map.",
      "file": "broken-inverted.stl", "units": "mm", "load": "ok",
      "is_manifold": true, "is_watertight": true,
      "is_orientation_consistent": true, "is_solid": false,
      "triangles": 12, "vertices": 8, "components": 1,
      "findings": { "inverted-orientation": 1 }
    },
    {
      "_why": "A closed cube plus an isolated triangle with a repeated vertex. Degeneracy is a finding, not a fatal defect: it contributes nothing to any ray test, so the mesh remains solid.",
      "file": "broken-zero-area.stl", "units": "mm", "load": "ok",
      "is_manifold": true, "is_watertight": true,
      "is_orientation_consistent": true, "is_solid": true,
      "triangles": 13, "components": 2,
      "findings": { "degenerate-triangle": 1 }
    },
    {
      "_why": "A cube plus an isolated triangle whose three vertices are exactly collinear. Detected by exact orient2d on all three coordinate-plane projections, never by an area threshold. Its three edges are boundaries.",
      "file": "broken-collinear.stl", "units": "mm", "load": "ok",
      "is_manifold": false, "is_watertight": false,
      "is_orientation_consistent": true, "is_solid": false,
      "triangles": 13, "components": 2,
      "findings": { "degenerate-triangle": 1, "boundary-edge": 3 }
    },
    {
      "_why": "Two coincident triangles with opposite windings. Every edge has exactly two consistently wound uses, so it is manifold and watertight, and it encloses exactly nothing.",
